{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the ordered triple \\((p, q, s)\\) for the circle equation \\(x^2 + y^2 - px - qy + s = 0\\) that passes through the vertices of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) with opposite vertices \\(A = (3,4)\\) and \\(C = (7,10)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the center and radius of the circle:**\n\n   Since \\(A\\) and \\(C\\) are opposite vertices of the rectangle, the center of the rectangle (and the circle) is the midpoint of the diagonal \\(AC\\). The midpoint \\(M\\) of \\(AC\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   M = \\left( \\frac{3+7}{2}, \\frac{4+10}{2} \\right) = (5, 7).\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the radius of the circle:**\n\n   The radius \\(r\\) of the circle is half the length of the diagonal \\(AC\\). The length of \\(AC\\) is:\n   \\[\n   AC = \\sqrt{(7-3)^2 + (10-4)^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 36} = \\sqrt{52} = 2\\sqrt{13}.\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the radius \\(r\\) is:\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{AC}{2} = \\sqrt{13}.\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":894,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,11457,23725,1124,1188,79,11,2804,11,274,10699,8,369,279,12671,23606,17767,87,61,17,488,379,61,17,481,17146,481,2804,88,488,274,284,220,15,57758,429,16211,1526,279,17228,315,279,22756,17767,1867,6484,57758,448,14002,17228,17767,32,284,320,18,11,19,10699,8,323,17767,34,284,320,22,11,16,15,10699,701,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,35,24308,279,4126,323,10578,315,279,12671,25,56177,256,8704,17767,32,57758,323,17767,34,57758,525,14002,17228,315,279,22756,11,279,4126,315,279,22756,320,437,279,12671,8,374,279,81963,315,279,37236,17767,1706,59,568,576,81963,17767,44,57758,315,17767,1706,57758,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,386,284,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,90,18,10,22,15170,17,2137,1124,37018,90,19,10,16,15,15170,17,92,1124,1291,8,284,320,20,11,220,22,4292,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,9885,279,10578,315,279,12